WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.370
We are back with my culinary bestie, Chef Pilar Valdes.

2
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.710
(audience cheering)

3
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.450
And she's here with a delicious meal

4
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:15.190
for your family that only takes seven minutes to make.

5
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.480
And to prove it to you,

6
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.910
we've got a timer set and we're gonna start the minute,

7
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.110
and I'm gonna say right now.

8
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:22.450
Pilar, what are we making today?

9
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:27.360
Okay. So we all have our go-to easy dinners, right?

10
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.960 line:15%
We have our stir fries, our egg dishes, our sandwiches,

11
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.960 line:15%
those are great options,

12
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.350
but sometimes you wanna jug things up a little bit.

13
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:41.240
So today we are making steamed mussels

14
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:46.130
in a butter and Dijon mustard sauce.

15
00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.640
It's like restaurant quality,

16
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.921
but only in seven minutes, as you shall see.

17
00:00:49.921 --> 00:00:51.008
(audience cheering)

18
00:00:51.008 --> 00:00:53.730
I love restaurant quality in seven minutes.

19
00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.180
So the first thing that we have in the pan over here,

20
00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.010
is some olive oil and butter.

21
00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.030
and that's nice and hot and melted,

22
00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.600
and you're gonna throw in some chopped garlic and shallots,

23
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.700
and that's gonna be the base of your sauce.

24
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.770
So you're gonna give that a good saute.

25
00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.250
You want a medium to high heat,

26
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.320
'cause again, seven minutes, here we go.

27
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.800
Season that little salt and pepper.

28
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:14.830
That's a little salt.

29
00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:15.940
Salt.

30
00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.150
Pepper.

31
00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:17.983
Yeah.

32
00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:20.103
I love that, so that's gonna go,

33
00:01:20.103 --> 00:01:24.520
and then you're gonna mix your white wine Dijon mustard.

34
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.883
How easy is that?

35
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.810
Give that a little good whisk.

36
00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:30.150
I love a whisk.

37
00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:34.040
Mini whisk at that, and you're gonna pour it into the pan.

38
00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.380
So what's gonna happen there,

39
00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.820
as soon as you pour it into the pan

40
00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:39.400
it's gonna infuse with the garlic and shallots,

41
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.950
and it's gonna stop the cooking so it's not gonna burn.

42
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.550 line:15%
That's gonna come up to a boil, Drew.

43
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.330 line:15%
I would throw the lid on there so it goes faster.

44
00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:49.440 line:15%
And while we're waiting for that to come up to boil,

45
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.180 line:15%
